# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROSW — repo-root ignore rules
#
# This repo holds multiple tools, each in its own folder under a tool root
# (today: brushes/{pipeline,vault,catalog,library,app},
# creative-writing/{vault,pipeline}, studio/{vault,pipeline} and
# plugins/ui-design/{catalog,maintenance}).
# Rules here apply repo-wide.
# The vault carries its own creative-writing/vault/.gitignore for
# Obsidian-specific state; that file still applies inside the vault.
# brushes/ carries two of its own: brushes/library/.gitignore and
# brushes/vault/.gitignore.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keys belong in ~/.rosw/keys.env, outside the repo (python docs/setup_keys.py).
# A legacy creative-writing/pipeline/.env may still exist on a clone. Never commit
# either; .env.example documents the shape instead.
keys.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
credentials.json
*_token
*.token
.netrc

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Pipeline run state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-run checkpoint dirs (idea/outline/draft/state.json). Scratch by design —
# a finished piece lands in the vault's _Idea_Library/, not here.
runs/

# ── Generated design systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# search.py --persist writes design-system/<project-slug>/ (MASTER.md,
# tokens.json, theme.css) under --output-dir, or under the CURRENT DIRECTORY
# when --output-dir is omitted. Run from this repo, a stray run would drop
# generated files into the repo, so they are ignored. Always pass --output-dir
# pointing outside it. Regenerate with:
#   python plugins/ui-design/catalog/scripts/search.py "<query>" --design-system --persist -p "<name>" --output-dir "<dir>"
# plugins/ui-design/.gitignore repeats this rule, because the plugin is published
# on its own and this file does not travel with it.
design-system/

# ── Catalog refresh staging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Candidates, fetched upstream inputs and diffs written by the
# ui-design-catalog-refresh skill under plugins/ui-design/maintenance/candidates/.
# Scratch by design: a candidate is reviewed, and only an approved one is copied
# into plugins/ui-design/catalog/data/. The skill regenerates it from upstream.
# Deliberately NOT ignored: plugins/ui-design/catalog/data/.google-font-refresh.incomplete.json.
# validate_data.py treats its presence as a failure signal for a partial
# refresh, so it is a tripwire, not a cache.
candidates/

# ── Harvested site captures ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Browser captures fed to `python plugins/ui-design/maintenance/harvest-site-tokens.py
# report captures/*.json`. Each describes one page of one site at one moment;
# it is input to a review, not catalog data (see plugins/ui-design/SOURCE-RESEARCH.md).
# Re-capture by running the extractor: `harvest-site-tokens.py show-extractor`.
captures/

# ── Build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# build_package.py regenerates the distributable zip from source at any time.
*.zip
dist/
build/

# ── Local AI / embedding caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# rag_index/index.json is a TF-IDF index of the whole vault, rebuilt with
# `python creative-writing/vault/tools/vault_search.py index`. It also records
# an absolute vault path, so it is machine-local by nature.
rag_index/
.rag/
.rag_index/
.smart-env/
.smart-connections/
embeddings/
*.embeddings.json
*.faiss
*.ann

# ── Studio outputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What a studio run made and the author kept. The note in studio/vault/ is the
# record of how; the files themselves are large and are not versioned here.
# studio/pipeline/runs/ is already covered by `runs/` above.
studio/assets/

# ── Brush library ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# brushes/library/ holds the original .brush and .brushset files. They ARE
# committed, through Git LFS (.gitattributes), and so is what is derived from
# them: brushes/catalog/, the vault notes, the tag sidecars and the previews.
# The `*.zip` rule above still applies there, which is why a set is stored as
# Name.brushset and never as Name.brushset.zip. The search index is covered by
# `rag_index/` above.
#
# A test sitting on a device (brushes/pipeline/device_tests.py) is one folder
# under brushes/device-tests/. The brush files built into it are scratch and
# are NOT committed: every rule below ignores what sits directly in a sitting's
# folder. Three things are kept, because no build can make them again:
#   manifest.json   which brushes went to the device, under which folder names
#                   (a new build draws new ones)
#   CHECKLIST.md    the page the answers were written on
#   returned/       what came back from the device: the only evidence there is
# The brush files in returned/ go through Git LFS (.gitattributes).
brushes/device-tests/*/*
!brushes/device-tests/*/manifest.json
!brushes/device-tests/*/CHECKLIST.md
!brushes/device-tests/*/returned/

# ── Obsidian machine-local state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The first block covers a vault opened at the repo root. The second covers
# every vault below it: a pattern with a slash in it is anchored to this file's
# folder, so the first block alone does not reach studio/vault/ or
# creative-writing/vault/. Each vault also carries its own .gitignore.
# data.json is where a plugin keeps its settings, API keys included.
**/.obsidian/workspace.json
**/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
**/.obsidian/cache
**/.obsidian/graph.json
**/.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
**/.obsidian/plugins/*/vectors/
**/.obsidian/trash/
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/graph.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
.trash/
.obsidian/trash/

# ── OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
